<article class="prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1>Transactions</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every dollar that moves is a transaction. The register is the list of them.</p>

  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
  <h2>Add and edit</h2>
  <p>On iPhone, tap <strong>+</strong>. On Mac, use <strong>Add Transaction</strong> or press ⌘N. Choose <strong>Outflow</strong> or <strong>Inflow</strong>, the account, and a category. Inflow to <strong>Ready to Assign</strong> is new money waiting to be assigned. Tap a row later to edit it.</p>
  <p>The payee and category are suggested from where you are and what you usually buy. You can change both before you save.</p>
  <p>One purchase can be split across more than one category. The parts add up to the amount on the row.</p>
    </div>
